# Sidecar digest pins — repo-owned, committed to git.
# Every line pins one downloaded sidecar release asset by its SHA-256 digest.
# Bumps are reviewed in PRs: changing a digest here changes what the release
# workflow is allowed to extract and execute, so the diff must name the new
# upstream version and cite the asset it came from.
# Upstream manifests (the fork's SHA256SUMS, Xray's .dgst files) are fetched at
# build time and kept as CORROBORATION ONLY — they prove upstream consistency
# but ship from the same origin as the asset, so they cannot vouch for it.
# These digests were computed from the pinned upstream assets and
# cross-checked against the upstream SHA256SUMS/.dgst files where those exist.
#
# Format: <lowercase hex sha256>  <filename>
c2d8bfff918755808781dfdeeb8581b6c91eb3a243d9a7b55483cfc0c0684d32  sing-box-1.14.2-windows-amd64.zip
2bb467039310452380958b821983d5bb4f78fb70a2583914e4bea8b011582b64  sing-box-1.14.2-windows-arm64.zip
2a07b66b2e18a67a066bc38c838fbe665a0acd312f2bf6ecf35df36b275adbc1  sing-box-1.14.3-lx.21-windows-amd64.zip
1d9fe7e6c956cf6438046eeb608952a0a8ad948ef4b0b360593768de8d3f3243  sing-box-1.14.3-lx.21-windows-arm64.zip
d004c39288ce9ada487c6f398c7c545f7d749e44bdfdd59dbc9f865afba4e1ad  Xray-windows-64.zip
